:: Memories Just Another Night [nobr]

/* Intro */
Tick… tick… tick… <br>
<br>
The sound of the clock echoes through the near pitch-black room, the only light coming from a laptop that illuminates the tired face of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span>, bags under her eyes as she gazes at the empty word document. <br>
<br>
Tick… tick… tick… <br>
<br>
She taps the table, mind fuzzy from lack of sleep and the pounding in her head as she tries to come up with a hook, some idea for an article that will blow away her readers. She needs to come up with some ideas before her meeting this afternoon, but her thoughts swirl around in her head, her worries elsewhere. <br>
<br>
Tick… tick… tick… <br>
<br>
The sound of the clock seems to get faster, more drawn out. Wait, is that the clock? <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span>’s eyes fly to the door, the handle turning slowly shortly after the sond of a key is being pulled out of the lock. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> sighs, sleep disappearing from her eyes as she leans back and looks at the door with a raised eyebrow. The door opens carefully, a short shadow steps inside before turning around, trying to shut the door without making a sound. There is a sigh of relief as the door shuts in near silence, but then the ticking is broken by <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> clearing her throat. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Shit!”</span> The boy jumps from the sound, dropping his bag as he turns in fear. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>, technically <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span>’s youngest son due to him being a few minutes younger than his twin brother, sighs once more in relief and grabs his chest upon seeing just his mother sitting in the darkness. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Geez mom, scared me to death.”</span> <br>

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "Connor",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Everyday",
            Mouth: "Smirk",
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah? Kinda like how you scared me when I found pillows stuffed under your blankets.”</span> She retorts. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> <span style="Color: Pink">chuckles, the laugh of someone who is both nervous and guilty, but not too worried.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Guilty. Sorry… Didn’t mean to scare you, friends just wanted to hang out so…”</span> He gives her that smile. <span style="Color: Pink">The smile he knows she can’t stay mad at, one of cute guilt that promises to learn from its mistake but never does.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Am I in trouble?”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> glares at him for a moment, knowing she should act the strict mom, but just can’t. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“No.”</span> She sighs, gripping her tired eyes, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You’re just lucky I found you and not your dad. After that last stunt you pulled, he’s on the brink of sending you to military school. Would it kill you to not be such a little shit?”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Language!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> laughs, walking over to his mom. He glances over at her empty list of article ideas and raising an eyebrow, before hugging her. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Why don’t you do an article on prepubescent delinquency? Then I can pretend to read it and have a ‘coming to the light’ moment to get dad off my ass?”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Language.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> rolls her eyes and chuckles. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“And I thought you liked my articles? Or was that another lie.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I love them.”</span> <span style="Color: Pink">He kisses his mom on the forehead, playing up the charm. She knows he is mainly doing it to get out of trouble but appreciates the effort.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“And I would never lie to you. Dad, sure, but that’s because I love watching him get pissed.”</span> He laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Maybe that’s why he hates me.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Your dad doesn’t hate you, he just…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> sighs, pinching the top of her nose, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He just doesn’t understand you. Some kids are just a little… rebellious.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“A little?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> replies, sounding almost offended, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I try to at least be above average in my rebelling. Have to since Carter’s such a damn stick in the mud. I mean, what 10-year-old color-codes his underwear drawer?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> laughs while <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> can’t hide her smirk. <span style="Color: Yellow">Then, suddenly, there is a sound in the distance. A switch being flicked. They both turn to the hallway and see a light on.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Shit, your dad’s awake. If he realizes you snuck out-”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> quickly begins to shover her son towards the bathroom. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Go in there and hide your shoes and bag. If he asks, just say you fell asleep in your clothes.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Or, I’ll just toss my clothes in the hamper and say I slept naked.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> whispers back with a smirk, <span style="Color: Pink">quickly undoing his jeans and yanking both them and his underwear down as he is shoved into the bathroom. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> rolls her eyes as he playfully moons her as she shuts the bathroom door and quickly returns to her laptop.</span> <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Continue">>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Whose up at this-?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span>’s husband, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Brandon</span>, walks into the living room, stopping as he sees his wife sitting behind her dim laptop, sipping some coffee. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh. You’re up early?”</span> He pauses, glancing her up and down before sighing, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Or you haven’t gone to sleep yet, have you?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> doesn’t respond, instead turning back to her empty word document and taking another long sip. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span>, we talked about this. The doctor said you need to start sleeping better or your headaches will just get worse. Did you even take your medicine last night?”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m fine. Just got some inspiration for my meeting later, wrote one hell of an article, you’ll have to read it after my editor touches it up. But don’t worry, I’m going to sleep before I go.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> chuckles, standing up and grabbing her husband by the collar and pulling him in for a very long kiss. When her hands start to wander lower, he tenses up a bit and pulls away. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Could help tire me out, if you want?”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alright, alright.”</span> He says with a laugh, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Point made. Just… promise me this won’t become a regular-!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> interrupts her husband by pushing him onto the couch, surprising the much larger man as she slips on top of him. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Woah! Haha, calm down. We don’t want to wake the boys. Must have written a pretty good article if you’re this fired up.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What can I say? News is my second passion, after one <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Brandon Kent</span>.”</span> She slips her hand under <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Brandon</span>’s shirt, keeping his eyes on her as the bathroom door slowly opens and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> walks out. <span style="Color: Pink">He pauses upon seeing what’s going on and has to stifle a laugh. He gives his mom two thumbs up before slinking off to his bedroom without a stitch of clothing.</span> <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Connor",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Naked",
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                    Eyes: "Tired",
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>
    /* Connor: Naked, Smirk, Tired */

    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Okay, okay!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Brandon</span> puts his hands up, pushing <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> away as he stands back up, his face red and hot. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sadly, I have to get ready for work. Chief will kill me if I’m late. I’m going to go get ready. Just… promise me you’ll take your medication and get some sleep? The boys were up late watching a movie, so they will probably sleep until after 10 and Callum should be able to handle things today anyway. So please, just focus on resting until your meeting later, okay?”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Fine. But you owe me after work!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> slaps her husband’s butt, rather roughly, and winks at him. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Go catch some bad guys, tiger.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Brandon</span> chuckles nervously, looking like he’s really regretting the fact that he has to get ready for work. He walks down the hallway flushed and mumbling. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> laughs to herself as he walks back into the room. Despite being so big and strong, he turns into a little kid again whenever she teases him like that. It’s one of the things she loves about him. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> walks back over to her laptop, document still empty. <br>
    <br>
    Tick… tick… tick… <br>
    <br>
    She sighs, closing it and as the headache starts to pulse at the back of her head again. She grimaces as she reaches into her purse and pulls out a bottle of medication. <br>
    <br>
    Tick… tick… tick… <br>
    <br>
    She reads the label <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Two pills, twice a day.”</span> Her doctor is going to be mad she’s skipped last night’s dose… along with a few others. <br>
    <br>
    Tick… tick… tick… <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh well.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lynda Kent</span> thinks as she takes two and downs them with the rest of her coffee, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I can deal with a few more headaches. Afterall, I get them so often now it feels like just another night…”</span> <br>
    <<set $Memories.push("Just Another Night")>>
    <br>
    [[End|Memories]]
<</linkreplace>>